  "scoring_guide": {
    "version": 4,
    "title": "How Investment Guide scoring works",
    "intro": "Point-sum suggestion guide for SP/SSP chip investment, separated by class (Attack / Defense / Support). Not a damage calculator. Close letters still need a human look — especially when terrain coverage or ship/theater options differ.",
    "overrides": [
      "Attack / Defense / Support use separate bands for stats, Move (MOV), weapon range/power, and shield.",
      "Buckets: Priority (S+/S), Strong (A+/A), Situational (B+/B), Low (C–E).",
      "Rarity adjustment: N −5, R −4, SR −2, SSR/UR 0 — lower rarities do not share SSR letters for free.",
      "Combat tags only (cap +2): One-Shot Killer, Land, Aerial Use, Tank, and other curated combat/niche tags. Flavor/series tags do not score.",
      "Terrain: Space+Land deploy starts at 0; +1 per extra deployable terrain (Atmospheric / Underwater); −2 if missing Land or Space. Move is scored separately.",
      "Warships are excluded from the MS boards (different investment role; ship choice is limited separately).",
      "Pure permanent ATK/DEF/HP/MOB passives do not also score ability points (already reflected in SP/SSP totals). Tension-gated abilities score 0.",
      "MAP ammo only (1 → +1; 2+ → +2). Higher-range weapon bonus ignored when max weapon range ≤ 3.",
      "GN Field / Positron Reflector passives award no ability points.",
      "Pilot recommended MS: Attack → Attack only; Support → Attack+Support; Defense → Defense only (official/linked pair always allowed).",
      "Reborns Gundam uses transformed-form stats when scoring."
    ],
    "gaps": [
      "Ability / linked-pilot quality are estimated from text patterns (not a full effect parser).",
      "MS↔warship boarding restrictions are not in master data; deployability is the proxy for limited ship/theater options.",
      "Debuff “level” 3–6 is mapped from DEF-debuff % bands.",
      "Pilot scoring still uses public How it works tables (no creator pilot sheet)."
    ]
  }
}
